---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About ShanghaiGuide"
  description="About ShanghaiGuide: an independent, locally-informed travel guide to Shanghai. Honest firsthand recommendations, no sponsored content. Updated regularly."
>
  <section class="bg-neutral-900 py-20 md:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-300">About</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-extrabold leading-none tracking-tight text-white md:text-6xl">
        About ShanghaiGuide
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-20 md:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
      <div class="prose prose-neutral max-w-none">
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-neutral-600">
          ShanghaiGuide is an independent travel guide built by people who know Shanghai intimately. Jamie Chen has lived in Shanghai for over a decade, first as a journalist covering China's urban transformation, then as a food and travel writer for publications across Asia. Every recommendation on this site comes from firsthand experience — meals eaten, neighborhoods walked, rooftop bars tested at sunset.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900">Meet the writer</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-neutral-600">
          Jamie Chen moved to Shanghai in 2014 intending to stay for one year. More than a decade later, she is still here — still discovering new noodle shops in the French Concession, still finding hidden rooftop bars in Jing'an, still getting lost in the Old City's alleyways. Before ShanghaiGuide, Jamie wrote for Time Out Shanghai, Lonely Planet, and various food and travel magazines. She has eaten at every restaurant recommended on this site (often multiple times), visited every attraction during both peak and off-peak hours, and personally tested every itinerary to make sure the timing works and the transport connections make sense.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900">Why we built this</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-neutral-600">
          Most Shanghai travel content online is either written by people who spent 48 hours here and regurgitated the same 10 tourist spots, or it is produced by large travel media companies whose business model is affiliate commissions, not honest recommendations.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-neutral-600">
          We wanted something different: a guide that reflects the Shanghai we actually live in and love. The one where the best soup dumpling joint is an unmarked door on a side street, where the most beautiful walk is through a neighborhood with no English signage, and where the most memorable night might start in a hidden speakeasy and end with street-side jianbing at 3 AM.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900">Our approach</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 space-y-6">
          <div class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="mt-1 flex h-8 w-8 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-brand-50 text-brand-600">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Firsthand only</h3>
              <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-500">We do not write about places we have not been to. Every restaurant, bar, attraction, and hotel in this guide has been personally visited and verified.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="mt-1 flex h-8 w-8 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-brand-50 text-brand-600">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">No sponsored content</h3>
              <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-500">We do not accept payment for listings or reviews. Our recommendations are based on quality alone. If something changes and a place goes downhill, we update or remove it.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="mt-1 flex h-8 w-8 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-brand-50 text-brand-600">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Regularly updated</h3>
              <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-500">Shanghai changes fast. Restaurants close, new bars open, Metro lines extend. We revisit and update our content continuously to keep it accurate.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-neutral-600">
          Have a tip, correction, or just want to say hello? We would love to hear from you. Reach us at <a href="mailto:hello@things-to-do-in-shanghai-china.com" class="text-brand-600 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-brand-700">hello@things-to-do-in-shanghai-china.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
